Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: retain legacy receive interface before MLO routing

On a multi-channel hwsim PHY, cfg80211 delivers broadcast management frames
to registered VIFs on multiple logical bands. Private VAPs advertise MLO
enabled in the data model, but their unset link ID is 255. Frequency-only
MLO lookup redirects each such notification to the same private BSS before
hostapd can reject the original off-channel interface. One probe request
therefore creates three distinct responses even with rx_mgmt.drv_priv set.

Require the existing validated MLO link ID before frequency-only redirection
under HWSIM_RADIO. Legacy notifications retain their registered interface
and the receive-frequency check rejects off-channel delivery. Preserve
explicit kernel link-ID dispatch, established MLO links and physical-driver
behavior. Do not deduplicate packets, change scan/steering timers or discard
legitimate repeated probe requests.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -2620,7 +2620,11 @@
         if (link_id != -1) {
             interface = wifi_hal_get_mld_interface_by_link_id(interface, link_id);
-        } else if (freq != 0) {
+        } else if (freq != 0
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+            && wifi_hal_get_mld_link_id(interface) != NL80211_DRV_LINK_ID_NA
+#endif
+        ) {
             interface = wifi_hal_get_mld_interface_by_freq(interface, freq);
         }
     }
 #endif // HOSTAPD_VERSION >= 211 && CONFIG_GENERIC_MLO
